From f5271c08c08bc394323756da9b9f0d87cf7a09f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:08:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(plugins): per-callback hook budgets and a host
 deadline/abandon signal for bounded hooks [daveey]

A turn-end pre_verify checker that makes bounded model calls (coach: judge 60s + confirm 90s) ran under the
global 30s plugins.hook_callback_timeout: the host abandoned it, suppressed the callback for 60s (the next
turn's check was skipped), and the abandoned worker went on to record a nudge the host had discarded.

- A callback may declare its own bound: callback.hermes_hook_timeout (clamped to 600s, bounded hooks only,
  never turns the threaded path on when the global timeout is 0).
- current_hook_call() exposes the host's HookCallBudget on the worker: remaining() and an abandoned Event set
  the moment the host stops waiting; a late finish is logged as 'result discarded'.
- Call identity falls back to session_id, so one session's running pre_verify doesn't skip another's.
